Normalize job titles and match them to the target roles of an Ideal Customer Profile.

Use only the provided text. If a title is too vague to classify, return null for that field.

For each title return:
- `index`: the index given below.
- `function`: one of {{ functions | join(", ") }}.
- `seniority`: one of intern, entry, senior_ic, manager, director, vp, c_level, owner
  (e.g. "Head of X" = director; "Lead" without reports = senior_ic; "Founder"/"Proprietor" = owner;
  "Chief X Officer" = c_level; "AVP" = vp).
- `matched_role_index`: index of the target role below whose function and scope best match this title, or null
  if none match.
- `role_type`: the matched role's role_type ("buyer" or "influencer") if the person's seniority is at or
  near that role's minimum; "none" if no role matches.

